<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin Mutschmann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1947</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin Mutschmann was a German textile manufacturer and Nazi official, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauleiter">Gauleiter</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> from 1925 and Reich governor of Saxony from 1933 to 1945. He controlled the state government, persecuted political opponents and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and failed to prepare <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>'s air-raid defences. Captured by the Soviets in 1945, he was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-mutschmann.jpg" alt="Martin Mutschmann" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leipzig_International_Fair_1937_(Martin_Mutschmann).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
